From d51a6a1681c9007f8e33d94efda55a848a5d89e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <acc@felkru.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:07:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 73/73] Settings close while the host has the settings file
 open

The host calls window.warpPanelCloseSettings() when it opens settings.toml or keybindings.yaml, which closes the settings tab. While the file stays open, opening settings asks the host (warpPanelSettingsFileOpen / warpPanelRequestSettings) to close the file first; the host then reopens settings at the requested page with window.warpPanelOpenSettingsPage(slug), so settings always show what the file says. The too-narrow settings message gets an Open settings file button at the bottom center.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
